  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "For how many values of $b$ does the quadratic $x^2-100x+b$ have two positive integer roots (not necessarily distinct)?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$50$ values.\n\nCount the unordered positive integer root pairs with sum $100$.",
      "worked": "Let the roots be $r$ and $s$, with $r\\le s$. By Vieta’s formulas,\n$$\\begin{align*}r+s&=100,\\\\rs&=b.\\end{align*}$$\nThe pairs are $(1,99),(2,98),\\ldots,(50,50)$, giving $50$ pairs. Their products are distinct: for $1\\le r<50$,\n$$\\begin{align*}(r+1)(99-r)-r(100-r)&=99-2r\\\\(r+1)(99-r)-r(100-r)&>0.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore there are $50$ possible values of $b$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 68
  },
